SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Art of Coexistence
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are
  Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199491\n\n6
 :00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nWhat does it mean for humans and wil
 dlife to thrive together in an increasingly interconnected world? Coincidi
 ng with the arrival of The Great Elephant Migration in Boston\, this 'Qu
 in Chat brings together visionary voices at the forefront of conservation\
 , research\, and environmental storytelling for an evening of compelling c
 onversation.\n\nModerated by 'Quin Co-Founder and philanthropist\, Sandy E
 dgerley\, together with Founder of The Great Elephant Migration\, Ruth Gan
 esh and leading scholar of human-wildlife coexistence\, Dr. Tarsh Thekaeka
 ra\, the discussion will explore the ideas driving one of the world's most
  ambitious conservation initiatives.\n\nFrom restoring critical habitats a
 nd protecting biodiversity to reimagining the relationship between people 
 and the natural world\, look forward to a conversation that examines how i
 nnovation\, collaboration\, and community are reshaping the future of cons
 ervation.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. 
 Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask 
 that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the
  event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199491
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
