BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-201348@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260922T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260922T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260922T183000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "The Cruelest Game" by Matthew Futterman
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are Con
 firmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/201348\n\nCeleb
 rate an unforgettable summer of tennis with an inside look at the game bey
 ond center court. Join acclaimed sports journalist and bestselling author 
 Matthew Futterman for his first Boston appearance on the book tour for The
  Cruelest Game\, an illuminating exploration of the ambition\, resilience\
 , and sacrifice required to succeed at the highest levels of professional 
 tennis. Through remarkable access and previously untold stories\, Futterma
 n pulls back the curtain on the sport to examine the immense pressures fac
 ing established champions and the next generation of players competing for
  their place among tennis’s elite.\n\nJoining Futterman in conversation 
 are former world No. 7 tennis player and Olympic silver medalist\, Tim May
 otte\, and The New Yorker staff writer\, Louisa Thomas\, who pens the publ
 ication’s Sporting Scene column. Together\, they will bring perspectives
  from the court and the press box to a wide-ranging conversation about pro
 fessional tennis at a pivotal moment. As familiar legends make way for a n
 ew generation of stars\, the evening will explore the changing landscape o
 f the sport\, the realities behind its most celebrated victories\, and the
  personal price of pursuing greatness on the world stage. \n\n*This event
  is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites
  and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be 
 made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/201348
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
